# Phase 18 ProcessQueue pull-idle cache and current-revision P18-V02 refresh — 2026-10-21T16:41:10Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Code revision: `8589f104` (`fix(consumer): cache process queue idle setting`)
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

## Source audit follow-up

The pinned Java `ProcessQueue` and `PopProcessQueue` each capture
`rocketmq.client.pull.pullMaxIdleTime` in separate static fields. Rust now
caches the ProcessQueue value on first Push startup or direct ProcessQueue use,
while POP retains its independent cache. An invalid first ProcessQueue value
remains cached as the class-equivalent initialization error. The regression
`process_queue_pull_idle_property_keeps_its_first_java_class_value` verifies
that later property reads do not replace the initial value. Phase 6, 11 and 18
compatibility maps record the cache lifetime and direct API disposition.

